# Managed by gt — edit .gt-repo.yaml, then run `gt repo sync`.
#
# What lydite lets merge without a human reading it. A change merges unread
# only when a single entry covers every path it touched and that entry's
# condition holds; everything else is referred.
#
# dependency-version-bump is derived from the dependabot: block. It lists only
# files lydite reads a version comparison from — never Cargo.toml or
# package.json, so an edit to one of those alone stays referred — and
# ecosystems lydite cannot read contribute nothing. Turn it off with
# lydite.exempt_dependency_bumps: false, and add repository-specific entries
# under lydite.exemptions.
#
# lydite reads this file from the base commit and refers any pull request that
# changes it, which then needs a `/lydite clear`. Keep such a pull request to
# this file alone.
